   {:url "https://schema.org/StatisticalPopulation",
    :logseq.property/description
    "A StatisticalPopulation is a set of instances of a certain given type that satisfy some set of constraints. The property [[populationType]] is used to specify the type. Any property that can be used on instances of that type can appear on the statistical population. For example, a [[StatisticalPopulation]] representing all [[Person]]s with a [[homeLocation]] of East Podunk California would be described by applying the appropriate [[homeLocation]] and [[populationType]] properties to a [[StatisticalPopulation]] item that stands for that set of people.\nThe properties [[numConstraints]] and [[constraintProperty]] are used to specify which of the populations properties are used to specify the population. Note that the sense of \"population\" used here is the general sense of a statistical\npopulation, and does not imply that the population consists of people. For example, a [[populationType]] of [[Event]] or [[NewsArticle]] could be used. See also [[Observation]], where a [[populationType]] such as [[Person]] or [[Event]] can be indicated directly. In most cases it may be better to use [[StatisticalVariable]] instead of [[StatisticalPopulation]]."},
   :build/class-extends [:Intangible],
   :build/class-properties [:populationType]},
  :EnergyEfficiencyEnumeration
  {:block/title "EnergyEfficiencyEnumeration",
   :build/properties
   {:url "https://schema.org/EnergyEfficiencyEnumeration",
    :logseq.property/description
    "Enumerates energy efficiency levels (also known as \"classes\" or \"ratings\") and certifications that are part of several international energy efficiency standards."},
   :build/class-extends [:Enumeration]},
  :Syllabus
  {:block/title "Syllabus",
   :build/properties
   {:url "https://schema.org/Syllabus",
    :logseq.property/description
    "A syllabus that describes the material covered in a course, often with several such sections per [[Course]] so that a distinct [[timeRequired]] can be provided for that section of the [[Course]]."},
   :build/class-extends [:LearningResource]},
  :CompoundPriceSpecification
  {:block/title "CompoundPriceSpecification",
   :build/properties
   {:url "https://schema.org/CompoundPriceSpecification",
    :logseq.property/description
    "A compound price specification is one that bundles multiple prices that all apply in combination for different dimensions of consumption. Use the name property of the attached unit price specification for indicating the dimension of a price component (e.g. \"electricity\" or \"final cleaning\")."},
   :build/class-extends [:PriceSpecification],
   :build/class-properties [:priceType :priceComponent]},
  :PaymentMethod
  {:block/title "PaymentMethod",
   :build/properties
   {:url "https://schema.org/PaymentMethod",
    :logseq.property/description
    "A payment method is a standardized procedure for transferring the monetary amount for a purchase. Payment methods are characterized by the legal and technical structures used, and by the organization or group carrying out the transaction. The following legacy values should be accepted:\n    \\n\\n* http://purl.org/goodrelations/v1#ByBankTransferInAdvance\\n* http://purl.org/goodrelations/v1#ByInvoice\\n* http://purl.org/goodrelations/v1#Cash\\n* http://purl.org/goodrelations/v1#CheckInAdvance\\n* http://purl.org/goodrelations/v1#COD\\n* http://purl.org/goodrelations/v1#DirectDebit\\n* http://purl.org/goodrelations/v1#GoogleCheckout\\n* http://purl.org/goodrelations/v1#PayPal\\n* http://purl.org/goodrelations/v1#PaySwarm\\n\\nStructured values are recommended for newer payment methods."},
   :build/class-extends [:Intangible],
   :build/class-properties [:paymentMethodType]},
  :DefenceEstablishment
  {:block/title "DefenceEstablishment",
   :build/properties
   {:url "https://schema.org/DefenceEstablishment",
    :logseq.property/description
    "A defence establishment, such as an army or navy base."},
   :build/class-extends [:GovernmentBuilding]},
  :LiquorStore
  {:block/title "LiquorStore",
   :build/properties
   {:url "https://schema.org/LiquorStore",
    :logseq.property/description
    "A shop that sells alcoholic drinks such as wine, beer, whisky and other spirits."},
   :build/class-extends [:Store]},
  :VirtualLocation
  {:block/title "VirtualLocation",
   :build/properties
   {:url "https://schema.org/VirtualLocation",
    :logseq.property/description
    "An online or virtual location for attending events. For example, one may attend an online seminar or educational event. While a virtual location may be used as the location of an event, virtual locations should not be confused with physical locations in the real world."},
   :build/class-extends [:Intangible]},
  :FlightReservation
  {:block/title "FlightReservation",
   :build/properties
   {:url "https://schema.org/FlightReservation",
    :logseq.property/description
    "A reservation for air travel.\\n\\nNote: This type is for information about actual reservations, e.g. in confirmation emails or HTML pages with individual confirmations of reservations. For offers of tickets, use [[Offer]]."},
   :build/class-extends [:Reservation],
   :build/class-properties
   [:boardingGroup
    :securityScreening
    :passengerPriorityStatus
    :passengerSequenceNumber]},
  :Game
  {:block/title "Game",
   :build/properties
   {:url "https://schema.org/Game",
    :logseq.property/description
    "The Game type represents things which are games. These are typically rule-governed recreational activities, e.g. role-playing games in which players assume the role of characters in a fictional setting."},
   :build/class-extends [:CreativeWork],
   :build/class-properties
   [:characterAttribute
    :numberOfPlayers
    :gameItem
    :gameLocation
    :quest]},
  :MedicalRiskEstimator
  {:block/title "MedicalRiskEstimator",
   :build/properties
   {:url "https://schema.org/MedicalRiskEstimator",
    :logseq.property/description
    "Any rule set or interactive tool for estimating the risk of developing a complication or condition."},
   :build/class-extends [:MedicalEntity],
   :build/class-properties [:estimatesRiskOf :includedRiskFactor]},
  :ChooseAction
  {:block/title "ChooseAction",
   :build/properties
   {:url "https://schema.org/ChooseAction",
    :logseq.property/description
    "The act of expressing a preference from a set of options or a large or unbounded set of choices/options."},
   :build/class-extends [:AssessAction],
   :build/class-properties [:actionOption]},
  :BusinessEntityType
  {:block/title "BusinessEntityType",
   :build/properties
   {:url "https://schema.org/BusinessEntityType",
    :logseq.property/description
    "A business entity type is a conceptual entity representing the legal form, the size, the main line of business, the position in the value chain, or any combination thereof, of an organization or business person.\\n\\nCommonly used values:\\n\\n* http://purl.org/goodrelations/v1#Business\\n* http://purl.org/goodrelations/v1#Enduser\\n* http://purl.org/goodrelations/v1#PublicInstitution\\n* http://purl.org/goodrelations/v1#Reseller\n    "},
   :build/class-extends [:Enumeration]},
  :SellAction
  {:block/title "SellAction",
   :build/properties
   {:url "https://schema.org/SellAction",
    :logseq.property/description
    "The act of taking money from a buyer in exchange for goods or services rendered. An agent sells an object, product, or service to a buyer for a price. Reciprocal of BuyAction."},
   :build/class-extends [:TradeAction],
   :build/class-properties [:buyer]},
  :PeopleAudience
  {:block/title "PeopleAudience",
   :build/properties
   {:url "https://schema.org/PeopleAudience",
    :logseq.property/description
    "A set of characteristics belonging to people, e.g. who compose an item's target audience."},
   :build/class-extends [:Audience],
   :build/class-properties
   [:suggestedGender
    :suggestedAge
    :requiredMaxAge
    :requiredMinAge
    :healthCondition
    :suggestedMinAge
    :suggestedMeasurement
    :suggestedMaxAge
    :requiredGender]},
  :NutritionInformation
  {:block/title "NutritionInformation",
   :build/properties
   {:url "https://schema.org/NutritionInformation",
    :logseq.property/description
    "Nutritional information about the recipe."},
   :build/class-extends [:StructuredValue],
   :build/class-properties
   [:saturatedFatContent
    :unsaturatedFatContent
    :sodiumContent
    :fatContent
    :transFatContent
    :servingSize
    :sugarContent
    :proteinContent
    :calories
    :carbohydrateContent
    :fiberContent
    :cholesterolContent]},
  :BoardingPolicyType
  {:block/title "BoardingPolicyType",
   :build/properties
   {:url "https://schema.org/BoardingPolicyType",
    :logseq.property/description
    "A type of boarding policy used by an airline."},
   :build/class-extends [:Enumeration]},
  :PoliceStation
  {:block/title "PoliceStation",
   :build/properties
   {:url "https://schema.org/PoliceStation",
    :logseq.property/description "A police station."},
   :build/class-extends [:CivicStructure :EmergencyService]},
  :Invoice
  {:block/title "Invoice",
   :build/properties
   {:url "https://schema.org/Invoice",
    :logseq.property/description
    "A statement of the money due for goods or services; a bill."},
   :build/class-extends [:Intangible],
   :build/class-properties
   [:paymentMethodId
    :minimumPaymentDue
    :scheduledPaymentDate
    :confirmationNumber
    :paymentMethod
    :provider
    :totalPaymentDue
    :paymentDueDate
    :accountId
    :broker
    :category
    :billingPeriod
    :customer
    :paymentStatus
    :referencesOrder]},
  :ResumeAction
  {:block/title "ResumeAction",
   :build/properties
   {:url "https://schema.org/ResumeAction",
    :logseq.property/description
    "The act of resuming a device or application which was formerly paused (e.g. resume music playback or resume a timer)."},
   :build/class-extends [:ControlAction]},
  :MensClothingStore
  {:block/title "MensClothingStore",
   :build/properties
   {:url "https://schema.org/MensClothingStore",
    :logseq.property/description "A men's clothing store."},
   :build/class-extends [:Store]},
  :EmergencyService
  {:block/title "EmergencyService",
   :build/properties
   {:url "https://schema.org/EmergencyService",
    :logseq.property/description
    "An emergency service, such as a fire station or ER."},
   :build/class-extends [:LocalBusiness]},
  :BusinessEvent
  {:block/title "BusinessEvent",
   :build/properties
   {:url "https://schema.org/BusinessEvent",
    :logseq.property/description "Event type: Business event."},
   :build/class-extends [:Event]},
  :CourseInstance
  {:block/title "CourseInstance",
   :build/properties
   {:url "https://schema.org/CourseInstance",
    :logseq.property/description
    "An instance of a [[Course]] which is distinct from other instances because it is offered at a different time or location or through different media or modes of study or to a specific section of students."},
   :build/class-extends [:Event],
   :build/class-properties
   [:instructor :courseSchedule :courseWorkload :courseMode]},
  :Protein
  {:block/title "Protein",
   :build/properties
   {:url "https://schema.org/Protein",
    :logseq.property/description
    "Protein is here used in its widest possible definition, as classes of amino acid based molecules. Amyloid-beta Protein in human (UniProt P05067), eukaryota (e.g. an OrthoDB group) or even a single molecule that one can point to are all of type :Protein. A protein can thus be a subclass of another protein, e.g. :Protein as a UniProt record can have multiple isoforms inside it which would also be :Protein. They can be imagined, synthetic, hypothetical or naturally occurring."},
   :build/class-extends [:BioChemEntity],
   :build/class-properties [:hasBioPolymerSequence]},
  :Newspaper
  {:block/title "Newspaper",
   :build/properties
   {:url "https://schema.org/Newspaper",
    :logseq.property/description
    "A publication containing information about varied topics that are pertinent to general information, a geographic area, or a specific subject matter (i.e. business, culture, education). Often published daily."},
   :build/class-extends [:Periodical]},
  :MedicalContraindication
  {:block/title "MedicalContraindication",
   :build/properties
   {:url "https://schema.org/MedicalContraindication",
    :logseq.property/description
    "A condition or factor that serves as a reason to withhold a certain medical therapy. Contraindications can be absolute (there are no reasonable circumstances for undertaking a course of action) or relative (the patient is at higher risk of complications, but these risks may be outweighed by other considerations or mitigated by other measures)."},
   :build/class-extends [:MedicalEntity]},
  :Gene
  {:block/title "Gene",
   :build/properties
   {:url "https://schema.org/Gene",
    :logseq.property/description
    "A discrete unit of inheritance which affects one or more biological traits (Source: [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gene](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gene)). Examples include FOXP2 (Forkhead box protein P2), SCARNA21 (small Cajal body-specific RNA 21), A- (agouti genotype)."},
   :build/class-extends [:BioChemEntity],
   :build/class-properties
   [:encodesBioChemEntity
    :expressedIn
    :alternativeOf
    :hasBioPolymerSequence]},
  :Residence
  {:block/title "Residence",
   :build/properties
   {:url "https://schema.org/Residence",
    :logseq.property/description "The place where a person lives."},
   :build/class-extends [:Place],
   :build/class-properties [:accommodationFloorPlan]},
  :MobilePhoneStore
  {:block/title "MobilePhoneStore",
   :build/properties
   {:url "https://schema.org/MobilePhoneStore",
    :logseq.property/description
    "A store that sells mobile phones and related accessories."},
   :build/class-extends [:Store]},
  :AggregateOffer
  {:block/title "AggregateOffer",
   :build/properties
   {:url "https://schema.org/AggregateOffer",
    :logseq.property/description
    "When a single product is associated with multiple offers (for example, the same pair of shoes is offered by different merchants), then AggregateOffer can be used.\\n\\nNote: AggregateOffers are normally expected to associate multiple offers that all share the same defined [[businessFunction]] value, or default to http://purl.org/goodrelations/v1#Sell if businessFunction is not explicitly defined."},
   :build/class-extends [:Offer],
   :build/class-properties [:highPrice :offers :lowPrice :offerCount]},
  :ProgramMembership
  {:block/title "ProgramMembership",
   :build/properties
   {:url "https://schema.org/ProgramMembership",
    :logseq.property/description
    "Used to describe membership in a loyalty programs (e.g. \"StarAliance\"), traveler clubs (e.g. \"AAA\"), purchase clubs (\"Safeway Club\"), etc."},
   :build/class-extends [:Intangible],
   :build/class-properties
   [:member
    :membershipNumber
    :program
    :membershipPointsEarned
    :hostingOrganization
    :programName]},
  :EventStatusType
  {:block/title "EventStatusType",
   :build/properties
   {:url "https://schema.org/EventStatusType",
    :logseq.property/description
    "EventStatusType is an enumeration type whose instances represent several states that an Event may be in."},
   :build/class-extends [:StatusEnumeration]},
  :PaymentService
  {:block/title "PaymentService",
   :build/properties
   {:url "https://schema.org/PaymentService",
    :logseq.property/description
    "A Service to transfer funds from a person or organization to a beneficiary person or organization."},
   :build/class-extends [:PaymentMethod :FinancialProduct]},
  :PreventionIndication
  {:block/title "PreventionIndication",
   :build/properties
   {:url "https://schema.org/PreventionIndication",
    :logseq.property/description
    "An indication for preventing an underlying condition, symptom, etc."},
   :build/class-extends [:MedicalIndication]},
  :MovieRentalStore
  {:block/title "MovieRentalStore",
   :build/properties
   {:url "https://schema.org/MovieRentalStore",
    :logseq.property/description "A movie rental store."},
   :build/class-extends [:Store]},
  :Church
  {:block/title "Church",
   :build/properties
   {:url "https://schema.org/Church",
    :logseq.property/description "A church."},
   :build/class-extends [:PlaceOfWorship]},
  :WarrantyScope
  {:block/title "WarrantyScope",
   :build/properties
   {:url "https://schema.org/WarrantyScope",
    :logseq.property/description
    "A range of services that will be provided to a customer free of charge in case of a defect or malfunction of a product.\\n\\nCommonly used values:\\n\\n* http://purl.org/goodrelations/v1#Labor-BringIn\\n* http://purl.org/goodrelations/v1#PartsAndLabor-BringIn\\n* http://purl.org/goodrelations/v1#PartsAndLabor-PickUp\n      "},
   :build/class-extends [:Enumeration]},
  :Manuscript
  {:block/title "Manuscript",
   :build/properties
   {:url "https://schema.org/Manuscript",
    :logseq.property/description
    "A book, document, or piece of music written by hand rather than typed or printed."},
   :build/class-extends [:CreativeWork]},
  :CollectionPage
  {:block/title "CollectionPage",
   :build/properties
   {:url "https://schema.org/CollectionPage",
    :logseq.property/description "Web page type: Collection page."},
   :build/class-extends [:WebPage]},
  :BrainStructure
  {:block/title "BrainStructure",
   :build/properties
   {:url "https://schema.org/BrainStructure",
    :logseq.property/description
    "Any anatomical structure which pertains to the soft nervous tissue functioning as the coordinating center of sensation and intellectual and nervous activity."},
   :build/class-extends [:AnatomicalStructure]},
  :City
  {:block/title "City",
   :build/properties
   {:url "https://schema.org/City",
    :logseq.property/description "A city or town."},
   :build/class-extends [:AdministrativeArea]},
  :RadioChannel
  {:block/title "RadioChannel",
   :build/properties
   {:url "https://schema.org/RadioChannel",
    :logseq.property/description
    "A unique instance of a radio BroadcastService on a CableOrSatelliteService lineup."},
   :build/class-extends [:BroadcastChannel]},
  :AchieveAction
  {:block/title "AchieveAction",
   :build/properties
   {:url "https://schema.org/AchieveAction",
    :logseq.property/description
    "The act of accomplishing something via previous efforts. It is an instantaneous action rather than an ongoing process."},
   :build/class-extends [:Action]},
  :Brand
  {:block/title "Brand",
   :build/properties
   {:url "https://schema.org/Brand",
    :logseq.property/description
    "A brand is a name used by an organization or business person for labeling a product, product group, or similar."},
   :build/class-extends [:Intangible],
   :build/class-properties [:review :slogan :logo :aggregateRating]},
  :BuyAction
  {:block/title "BuyAction",
   :build/properties
   {:url "https://schema.org/BuyAction",
    :logseq.property/description
    "The act of giving money to a seller in exchange for goods or services rendered. An agent buys an object, product, or service from a seller for a price. Reciprocal of SellAction."},
   :build/class-extends [:TradeAction],
   :build/class-properties [:seller]},
  :NonprofitType
  {:block/title "NonprofitType",
   :build/properties
   {:url "https://schema.org/NonprofitType",
    :logseq.property/description
    "NonprofitType enumerates several kinds of official non-profit types of which a non-profit organization can be."},
   :build/class-extends [:Enumeration]},
  :MedicalTest
  {:block/title "MedicalTest",
   :build/properties
   {:url "https://schema.org/MedicalTest",
    :logseq.property/description
    "Any medical test, typically performed for diagnostic purposes."},
   :build/class-extends [:MedicalEntity],
   :build/class-properties
   [:usedToDiagnose
    :normalRange
    :affectedBy
    :signDetected
    :usesDevice]},
  :FinancialService
  {:block/title "FinancialService",
   :build/properties
   {:url "https://schema.org/FinancialService",
    :logseq.property/description "Financial services business."},
   :build/class-extends [:LocalBusiness],
   :build/class-properties [:feesAndCommissionsSpecification]},
  :IPTCDigitalSourceEnumeration
  {:block/title "IPTCDigitalSourceEnumeration",
   :build/properties
   {:url "https://schema.org/IPTCDigitalSourceEnumeration",
    :logseq.property/description
    "<a href=\"https://www.iptc.org/\">IPTC</a> \"Digital Source\" codes for use with the [[digitalSourceType]] property, providing information about the source for a digital media object.\nIn general these codes are not declared here to be mutually exclusive, although some combinations would be contradictory if applied simultaneously, or might be considered mutually incompatible by upstream maintainers of the definitions. See the IPTC <a href=\"https://www.iptc.org/std/photometadata/documentation/userguide/\">documentation</a>\n for <a href=\"https://cv.iptc.org/newscodes/digitalsourcetype/\">detailed definitions</a> of all terms."},
   :build/class-extends [:MediaEnumeration]},
  :EducationalOccupationalCredential
  {:block/title "EducationalOccupationalCredential",
   :build/properties
   {:url "https://schema.org/EducationalOccupationalCredential",
    :logseq.property/description
    "An educational or occupational credential. A diploma, academic degree, certification, qualification, badge, etc., that may be awarded to a person or other entity that meets the requirements defined by the credentialer."},
   :build/class-extends [:CreativeWork],
   :build/class-properties
   [:recognizedBy
    :credentialCategory
    :validFor
    :educationalLevel
    :competencyRequired
    :validIn]},
  :EventAttendanceModeEnumeration
  {:block/title "EventAttendanceModeEnumeration",
   :build/properties
   {:url "https://schema.org/EventAttendanceModeEnumeration",
    :logseq.property/description
    "An EventAttendanceModeEnumeration value is one of potentially several modes of organising an event, relating to whether it is online or offline."},
   :build/class-extends [:Enumeration]},
  :PhysicalExam
  {:block/title "PhysicalExam",
   :build/properties
   {:url "https://schema.org/PhysicalExam",
    :logseq.property/description
    "A type of physical examination of a patient performed by a physician. "},
   :build/class-extends [:MedicalEnumeration :MedicalProcedure]},
  :MedicalCode
  {:block/title "MedicalCode",
   :build/properties
   {:url "https://schema.org/MedicalCode",
    :logseq.property/description "A code for a medical entity."},
   :build/class-extends [:MedicalIntangible :CategoryCode],
   :build/class-properties [:codingSystem :codeValue]},
  :RegisterAction
  {:block/title "RegisterAction",
   :build/properties
   {:url "https://schema.org/RegisterAction",
    :logseq.property/description
    "The act of registering to be a user of a service, product or web page.\\n\\nRelated actions:\\n\\n* [[JoinAction]]: Unlike JoinAction, RegisterAction implies you are registering to be a user of a service, *not* a group/team of people.\\n* [[FollowAction]]: Unlike FollowAction, RegisterAction doesn't imply that the agent is expecting to poll for updates from the object.\\n* [[SubscribeAction]]: Unlike SubscribeAction, RegisterAction doesn't imply that the agent is expecting updates from the object."},
   :build/class-extends [:InteractAction]},
  :DeliveryMethod
  {:block/title "DeliveryMethod",
   :build/properties
   {:url "https://schema.org/DeliveryMethod",
    :logseq.property/description
    "A delivery method is a standardized procedure for transferring the product or service to the destination of fulfillment chosen by the customer. Delivery methods are characterized by the means of transportation used, and by the organization or group that is the contracting party for the sending organization or person.\\n\\nCommonly used values:\\n\\n* http://purl.org/goodrelations/v1#DeliveryModeDirectDownload\\n* http://purl.org/goodrelations/v1#DeliveryModeFreight\\n* http://purl.org/goodrelations/v1#DeliveryModeMail\\n* http://purl.org/goodrelations/v1#DeliveryModeOwnFleet\\n* http://purl.org/goodrelations/v1#DeliveryModePickUp\\n* http://purl.org/goodrelations/v1#DHL\\n* http://purl.org/goodrelations/v1#FederalExpress\\n* http://purl.org/goodrelations/v1#UPS\n        "},
   :build/class-extends [:Enumeration]},
  :AccountingService
  {:block/title "AccountingService",
   :build/properties
   {:url "https://schema.org/AccountingService",
    :logseq.property/description
    "Accountancy business.\\n\\nAs a [[LocalBusiness]] it can be described as a [[provider]] of one or more [[Service]]\\(s).\n      "},
   :build/class-extends [:FinancialService]},
  :FinancialIncentive
  {:block/title "FinancialIncentive",
   :build/properties
   {:url "https://schema.org/FinancialIncentive",
    :logseq.property/description
    "<p>Represents financial incentives for goods/services offered by an organization (or individual).</p>\n\n<p>Typically contains the [[name]] of the incentive, the [[incentivizedItem]], the [[incentiveAmount]], the [[incentiveStatus]], [[incentiveType]], the [[provider]] of the incentive, and [[eligibleWithSupplier]].</p>\n\n<p>Optionally contains criteria on whether the incentive is limited based on [[purchaseType]], [[purchasePriceLimit]], [[incomeLimit]], and the [[qualifiedExpense]].\n    "},
   :build/class-extends [:Intangible],
   :build/class-properties
   [:incentivizedItem
    :purchasePriceLimit
    :incentiveStatus
    :purchaseType
    :provider
    :validFrom
    :areaServed
    :eligibleWithSupplier
    :qualifiedExpense
    :incentiveAmount
    :incentiveType
    :incomeLimit
    :publisher
    :validThrough]},
  :Room
  {:block/title "Room",
   :build/properties
   {:url "https://schema.org/Room",
    :logseq.property/description
    "A room is a distinguishable space within a structure, usually separated from other spaces by interior walls (source: Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia, see <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Room\">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Room</a>).\n<br /><br />\nSee also the <a href=\"https://schema.org/docs/hotels.html\">dedicated document on the use of schema.org for marking up hotels and other forms of accommodations</a>.\n"},
   :build/class-extends [:Accommodation]},
  :MemberProgramTier
  {:block/title "MemberProgramTier",
   :build/properties
   {:url "https://schema.org/MemberProgramTier",
    :logseq.property/description
